Is the claim supported by the evidence? A claim counts as supported only if the evidence warrants it as stated, including its degree of certainty, whether it asserts causation or only association, and its scope (population, setting, quantifier). A claim stated more strongly or more generally than the evidence warrants is NOT supported. A claim stated more cautiously than the evidence is still supported. Answer Yes or No.
